n/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9ca9e56-ab61-56bb-8369-2b3458fa57a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-38581" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c62bf5398a58cf3e27b3a47f4494fccc6d89e453685d1cd8620588c3d2bb2fa.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is odd, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, statement “The coefficient of the leading term is positive” is false, while statements “$P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$” and “The degree of $P(x)$ is odd” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050601 :topic/id #uuid "577aebce-a9af-5bcd-867f-fb32f559c852" :topic/math-academy-id 2049 :topic/title "Graphing General Polynomials"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "834b4bf2-1b3f-5d4c-b491-7c02c93b219d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438272} {:answer/id #uuid "0d78d218-e768-5739-88e2-395aa7b97bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d78d218-e768-5739-88e2-395aa7b97bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438273} :answer-field/id #uuid "3261d56f-16e4-5e60-975f-57584426806f" :answer-field/key "$p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23eb9a8c-3df5-5681-8e74-07043805cab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438274} {:answer/id #uuid "049c70be-8905-50c7-afdd-44a53874517c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23eb9a8c-3df5-5681-8e74-07043805cab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438274} :answer-field/id #uuid "742164e8-41f0-546c-b779-b81e59044b5b" :answer-field/key "$x=-1$ is a simple root." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db18b8f2-ea83-5fef-a642-7bbba6480576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438276} {:answer/id #uuid "80d5c6ad-057f-53d5-b496-f302316f61f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db18b8f2-ea83-5fef-a642-7bbba6480576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438276} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fc05ecc-740b-590b-bb06-34ae388c9b15" :answer-field/key "$x=2$ is a root of even multiplicity." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f729aa18-847a-50e3-929f-e0ca720e3184" :question/math-academy-id "q-38680" :question/problem "![](images/68/682105815047990048e100ea59c2652e48c0deea8c8caa422bfe3efca7d11c65.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are correct?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$” is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement “$x=-1$ is a simple root” is false. The root $x=-1$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement “$x=2$ is a root of even multiplicity” is false. The root $x=2$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050601 :topic/id #uuid "577aebce-a9af-5bcd-867f-fb32f559c852" :topic/math-academy-id 2049 :topic/title "Graphing General Polynomials"} :activity/title "Graphing General Polynomials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574946} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575659}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07b63c0c-daaa-5f5b-acb3-58d6f36ee869" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Jump Discontinuity on a Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050124 :topic/id #uuid "2eb940a7-12ca-5de2-9f75-d2efec304289" :topic/math-academy-id 2003 :topic/title "Jump Discontinuities"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "300eabc4-340c-5c3d-aeb2-845ce444c28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467422} {:answer/id #uuid "d83f5d6b-c310-5fa4-8838-8f8978fab1a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83f5d6b-c310-5fa4-8838-8f8978fab1a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467423} :answer-field/id #uuid "809ca4e9-905a-5156-b1d5-d4ce4e4cca06" :answer-field/key "It has a jump discontinuity at $x=2.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468432} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "169741b5-c91a-54f4-bc02-86818eaba819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467424} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5321df-f532-5a02-8b1b-4341a87f294c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "169741b5-c91a-54f4-bc02-86818eaba819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467424} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d534751-3db5-590e-b190-d141f3e4acb7" :answer-field/key "It has a point discontinuity at $x=2.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468433} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1e6937-b452-55e5-b9fc-00a00b1d591b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467426} {:answer/id #uuid "bccdef66-e2a6-5586-ac1f-e6264f5d9bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f1e6937-b452-55e5-b9fc-00a00b1d591b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467426} :answer-field/id #uuid "93403f72-4436-5cda-9b11-22784905428c" :answer-field/key "It is continuous at $x=2.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54b552a9-f11b-599e-8e55-508447a23c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-38712" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a9a1be6abdaf5104cecf7544dc77687db2892de1e3b39faab03f99b84003c03.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=2.$ Checking our conditions, we see that\n\n- $f(2)=2$ exists, $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)=2,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=3.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=2$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, “It has a jump discontinuity at $x=2.$” is true, and “It has a point discontinuity at $x=2.$” and “It is continuous at $x=2.$” are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129148 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34aa8f4e-20f1-5dda-ac53-6eb411543897" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050046 :topic/id #uuid "288ef1bc-9e03-59cc-957a-e1edeebef5c3" :topic/math-academy-id 2050 :topic/title "End Behavior of Polynomials"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dae4896a-777c-5d19-b424-351ccc57c7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/id