:answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5188349b-4c96-553c-a9c2-bb2336ff508e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40799" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of $f(x)=-{(2)}^{-x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The range of ${2}^{-x}$ is\n\n$$\n{2}^{-x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1){(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ -{(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ f(x) & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<0.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-0.5$ is an output of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/95/95ad3043259402375e7b5822aef88d77027222a3372c2b8ab042d1b54e08666f.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The number $-0.5$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048980 :topic/id #uuid "d0f342d9-c70c-537f-9e04-f3b0beaf9c01" :topic/math-academy-id 2083 :topic/title "Row Echelon Form"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82ceb6ee-967f-51f6-9562-a946e9616bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} {:answer/id #uuid "5a978d2b-7bde-5c45-a243-0e4e0a33fde7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82ceb6ee-967f-51f6-9562-a946e9616bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} :answer-field/id #uuid "f80dcb05-a2c2-516d-80fe-1ab0eed4e12b" :answer-field/key "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b08f801-3599-510d-8753-6582f23b7efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} {:answer/id #uuid "62d0a2f4-51a8-5771-9041-0b5950520f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b08f801-3599-510d-8753-6582f23b7efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4a18d9-f146-57c1-98ce-7671782922ed" :answer-field/key "$B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468466} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ed2b63-95a4-56b7-afb2-010d21ef08ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467492} {:answer/id #uuid "158e4809-5e64-50a5-af3e-ca976103a4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158e4809-5e64-50a5-af3e-ca976103a4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bbb80cd-ffa5-5028-b638-d29609a12eae" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "324c0e93-0bc4-5958-ba8a-b87ad1b81b6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42028" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050283 :topic/id #uuid "3cb2a10b-5d06-5efe-b222-3c14b0ccd7c8" :topic/math-academy-id 1777 :topic/title "Triangular Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c6bb28-f335-5bbd-98ef-7c10debcd116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438308} {:answer/id #uuid "f443bd43-943d-5991-a1db-7e129b593206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f443bd43-943d-5991-a1db-7e129b593206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438309} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe78ff6-d1f1-58f5-8add-6b463affc7cc" :answer-field/key "$A$ is lower triangular." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07dc0e6-51e2-5ce8-a1b4-44727450bef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438310} {:answer/id #uuid "cef77811-df7c-59ed-a36f-ed5228a3ebc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07dc0e6-51e2-5ce8-a1b4-44727450bef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438310} :answer-field/id #uuid "371815f8-f16e-5680-9ce5-31f3cff1d9be" :answer-field/key "${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439184} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76c420bb-1528-5dc2-9b89-925a5134c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438312} {:answer/id #uuid "f06b9547-425a-5254-b4f6-2c95fe1f7d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c420bb-1528-5dc2-9b89-925a5134c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438312} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ba6e7f7-ddb2-5a5c-9829-6eb52ab534d3" :answer-field/key "$A$ is upper triangular." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7fc84187-05b2-57ce-8e48-261250d11c80" :question/math-academy-id "q-42116" :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular: **False.** This fails because the result of ${A}^{T}-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048221 :topic/id #uuid "8959dd0b-8ef2-54bf-b8d9-d9b2606263cd" :topic/math-academy-id 1735 :topic/title "Partitioned and Block Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195c361c-f98a-56bc-95a9-a24d6ae95142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467494} {:answer/id #uuid "087e2b8e-167a-55dd-a33c-443fc10c0a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "087e2b8e-167a-55dd-a33c-443fc10c0a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467495} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bcb8c2f-2a00-55cd-bda8-3dffe1628a2f" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468468} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010a0770-3fce-59e2-86e4-c29d912931fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467496} {:answer/id #uuid "7127439e-6346-576e-adcf-02d5a6d602d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7127439e-6346-576e-adcf-02d5a6d602d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467497} :answer-field/id #uuid "e04e0008-7373-571f-9da6-ce0524c094b7" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468469} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33c9ca18-0830-5bb9-94a9-9ae66555b1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467498} {:answer/id #uuid "095d4e7f-7b52-523f-ae5b-6a414007ba1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33c9ca18-0830-5bb9-94a9-9ae66555b1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467498} :answer-field/id #uuid "82277b7d-af0a-5d41-83d1-80cb091465ec" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "366fb16a-48e3-5635-add3-b8c862272224" :question/math-academy-id "q-42127" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block lower triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $B$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048221 :topic/id #uuid "8959dd0b-8ef2-54bf-b8d9-d9b2606263cd" :topic/math-academy-id 1735 :topic/title "Partitioned and Block Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf81b5d0-b61e-5203-bb54-801438d3461d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} {:answer/id #uuid "fd171565-81f8-50d3-8a91-05948557c95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf81b5d0-b61e-5203-bb54-801438d3461d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a853d7c-2687-518d-a446-c138652f4c7e" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468471} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc4d0664-5482-5544-9e91-690f058f2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} {:answer/id #uuid "12bbe01a-fe98-5ec1-a6c8-24a6cbbe1cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc4d0664-5482-5544-9e91-690f058f2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} :answer-field/id #uuid "34b3dc6c-709b-5dee-acff-ac14c1ddc707" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "825129c8-74ee-54bf-8b70-10f615c4071d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} {:answer/id #uuid "35dfa222-4364-5bbd-af7c-c6cfea240e47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "825129c8-74ee-54bf-8b70-10f615c4071d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5535032e-f5c6-5f9b-b4e5-bbd70b524e51" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1e9c127-3ff2-5d29-89f3-9a02b595895a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42138" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block upper triangular?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block upper triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks below the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050122 :topic/id #uuid "2eaec2b9-4c03-5efd-b5aa-8e9655cca4f4" :topic/math-academy-id 1724 :topic/title "Properties of Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98d094e2-1177-5e99-96ad-7caeee897640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450618} {:answer/id #uuid "ca99c815-da6d-51d7-a07d-611d7659f788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98d094e2-1177-5e99-96ad-7caeee897640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450618} :answer-field/id #uuid "c30fd7ce-bd14-59fb-ab10-845f8a59bb92" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956b7a25-6517-5ef2-837c-39c50a5c5a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450620} {:answer/id #uuid "bd63bdd4-4b06-56ad-b67b-a613cc1dd46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd63bdd4-4b06-56ad-b67b-a613cc1dd46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450621} :answer-field/id #uuid "382ec9ba-1720-5328-8c38-f194ab93dcab" :answer-field/key "$(AB)C=A(BC)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451264} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "762ad639-2afc-55e3-bdc7-be4e7057c714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450622} {:answer/id #uuid "7a78eef3-ff9c-56b5-98cb-545a4b324d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "762ad639-2afc-55e3-bdc7-be4e7057c714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450622} :answer-field/id #uuid "800a3551-29f1-5bb8-a3bc-66ca201c01c9" :answer-field/key "$A(B-C)=(B-C)A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "005a0156-3d99-59d1-ab99-adf9b9b4c7b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42264" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $AB=BA$ is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement $(AB)C=A(BC)$ is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement $A(B-C)=(B-C)A$ is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $A(B-C)\\ne (B-C)A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement $(AB)C=A(BC)$ is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050122 :topic/id #uuid "2eaec2b9-4c03-5efd-b5aa-8e9655cca4f4" :topic/math-academy-id 1724 :topic/title "Properties of Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ede5fc7-4e98-54a5-a8b6-e3d24c4c38db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450624} {:answer/id #uuid "55e4960c-b4a8-5dc4-9358-5474cf82f7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ede5fc7-4e98-54a5-a8b6-e3d24c4c38db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450624} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5404b0-68d0-5679-9acd-82c4cfdc5828" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7725433-91f4-58a8-86f9-aeb838dcca83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450626} {:answer/id #uuid "db204d99-d48d-5b15-a94d-fd45955b1ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db204d99-d48d-5b15-a94d-fd45955b1ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450627} :answer-field/id #uuid "36d78dc9-a409-525c-846b-1acf74456b6c" :answer-field/key "$A(B+C)=AB+AC$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451267} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6be3f3c0-0d5f-53d8-b5d4-1cdbc4330e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450628} {:answer/id #uuid "32dd403d-28b4-5b42-93d6-1c1a8a1630d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32dd403d-28b4-5b42-93d6-1c1a8a1630d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450629} :answer-field/id #uuid "baab8b40-76af-5c21-b0d3-f31812f8c1dd" :answer-field/key "$B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cea2f24d-948b-5d70-91c6-23df57186795" :question/math-academy-id "q-42267" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $5\\times 5$ matrices, and  ${I}_{5}$ is the $5\\times 5$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $AB=BA$ is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement $B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B$ is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B=B.$\n\nTherefore, only statements $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ and $B{I}_{5}={I}_{5}B$ are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329644 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/id #uuid "be557898-2dc0-5c08-b4e7-63bbb4f08f56" :topic/math-academy-id 1198 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e232d15-a82e-5bae-ad4e-7151f902a03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450630} {:answer/id #uuid "016d62d0-b45f-56de-ac7a-54959e9d1014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e232d15-a82e-5bae-ad4e-7151f902a03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450630} :answer-field/id #uuid "69857d61-3c1e-5f25-b16c-ae8c4b26a97b" :answer-field/key "The product $JK$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b72976-dc85-5a33-9be2-c83670ec7e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450632} {:answer/id #uuid "283d41dd-3b3f-5bd7-9eed-4933fde66ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283d41dd-3b3f-5bd7-9eed-4933fde66ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450633} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cf63d8-da92-5363-889b-bd55efe17b6d" :answer-field/key "The product $KL$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caca7f8a-73a6-5713-9718-8a9f3a6ffce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450634} {:answer/id #uuid "38fd2b25-e69d-5619-b54c-39f7cb6d92d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caca7f8a-73a6-5713-9718-8a9f3a6ffce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450634} :answer-field/id #uuid "67959733-2425-566d-8885-d0d38ff4a97c" :answer-field/key "The product $JL$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e92499c-048f-53fc-971b-21b3cc496d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42375" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$J=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$K=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $J,K,$ and $L?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $J$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $L$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $J$ and $3$ rows in $K.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $K,$ the matrices $J$ and $K$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{K}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $K$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $K$ equals the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $K$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{K}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $J$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $J$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe product $KL$ is well defined. The products $JK$ and $JL$ are undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/id #uuid "be557898-2dc0-5c08-b4e7-63bbb4f08f56" :topic/math-academy-id 1198 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2471c953-6866-5f30-b8fb-642d99c1ace1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450636} {:answer/id #uuid "1416b89a-9a9c-5884-826f-ae30875cf015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1416b89a-9a9c-5884-826f-ae30875cf015" :answer/type {:db/id 