{:answer/id #uuid "5ddcb0bf-22bc-580a-9f9f-9c09ea70ffbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438318} {:answer/id #uuid "b8110f84-150f-541f-b756-551b0e23ad1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ddcb0bf-22bc-580a-9f9f-9c09ea70ffbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438318} :answer-field/id #uuid "33037cbe-1756-5c5e-b354-7c66976c18f6" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18223e97-17ad-509c-a688-bf8d869b747a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48040" :question/problem "![](images/59/59c02273515e87fcebb8eb1785dc2cf0c6490feda4fc9644df43b8849921eec5.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$” is true. The function $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$ and we have $f(-1)=1.$\n\n- Statement “${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ exists” is false. We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, both left-hand side and right-hand side limits exist but they are not the same. Therefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$” is false. The function contains a break exactly at $x=-1$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8e886b-57f2-59c5-b759-e8c984922226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae70a57b-88e6-5264-9484-75fdbfb3d260" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is defined at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c504c9e2-a62c-527b-a9e7-002c0a5d6492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438328} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d2fa27-53f5-5bde-85b6-c4f96e3a4c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d2fa27-53f5-5bde-85b6-c4f96e3a4c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438329} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ed00390-f87b-59cf-b29a-87e97f2baa99" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)$ exists" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd6d307-6b90-5d32-8396-2192f0a65d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438330} {:answer/id #uuid "278fac04-a440-5c31-bf6f-e56fa749884f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bd6d307-6b90-5d32-8396-2192f0a65d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438330} :answer-field/id #uuid "4150e66a-c62a-5f54-84bd-4cbabf0439eb" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96069899-bca3-51de-b64c-6e29072ea13e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48062" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9db7f2a491ae3065dbe8434a71d378c4fed8fec16c82e2fd76dcb209c786809.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=1$” is false. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement “${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)$ exists” is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=1.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$” is false. The function is not even defined at $x=1.$ The graph contains a break at $x=1.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cea1630d-9468-583c-91a2-a690bea97b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438332} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8b497a-fca1-5731-b90f-85bab2f82f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8b497a-fca1-5731-b90f-85bab2f82f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438333} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6a329d-7e8b-5bbe-84ab-3637480764d6" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a5a274-c228-5909-99ce-c54b27b6c8ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438334} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f9a903-77ef-594e-8ef5-a0c888c75c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8f9a903-77ef-594e-8ef5-a0c888c75c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438335} :answer-field/id #uuid "89ad00f4-8b1c-5a88-a148-6fa4641c1832" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=f(2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f597ecb7-ffec-5721-b982-5b030db741d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438336} {:answer/id #uuid "c891c5b7-7456-534a-9fcd-2f30724d3718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c891c5b7-7456-534a-9fcd-2f30724d3718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438337} :answer-field/id #uuid "87229505-3eea-5206-972c-e5c0c558ab4b" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e01edc7-98f4-52fe-bf43-cb1e05ae0d4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48065" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa15192923f9fd7370818fcb6b05b24b3bb6901dfbf90dd53539d71fd0f8b0bf.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$” is true. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$ and $f(2)=1.$\n\n- Statement ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=f(2)$ is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=1=f(2).$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$” is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329856 :knowledge-point/_questions 